{"id": "DeBaajzgEeb", "title": "Video by academaai", "description": "Training an AI to Drive with Natural Selection\n\nA self-driving car does what you do, many times a second: look, decide, act. Looking turns the road into numbers (how far is that wall? how fast am I going?). Deciding is a function that turns those numbers into gas, brake and steering.\n\nThis car sees seven numbers: how far the walls are along five yellow lines, its speed, and its direction. Its function is a small neural network with 434 weights, and nobody set them. I made twenty random ones and let them race; most crashed at once. The ones that got furthest became parents, and their children are copies with small random changes. Generation 33 finished the first lap. By generation 4,000 they race through every corner, on lines they found themselves.\n\nIn the literature this is called neuroevolution: a neural network trained by selection and mutation alone, with no gradients.\n\n#AI #neuralnetwork #evolution #selfdriving #machinelearning", "channel": "academaai", "uploader_id": "46925220748", "uploader": "Academa", "timestamp": 1791008862, "like_count": 41688, "comment_count": 307, "http_headers": {"User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/151.0.0.0 Safari/537.36", "Accept": "text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9,*/*;q=0.8", "Accept-Language": "en-us,en;q=0.5", "Sec-Fetch-Mode": "navigate", "Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-18073145804564749a", "manifest_url": null, "ext": "m4a", "width": null, "height": null, "tbr": 63.824, "asr": 48000, "fps": null, "language": null, "format_note": "DASH audio", "filesize": null, "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "dynamic_range": null, "url": "https://scontent-sjc6-1.cdninstagram.com/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQP9Cq0OAeqdpRKKD_8vSo6KULYIYw53tCEDlaNu9RS5ig5Nksm7LmW5HI_WGYFwZTdJ9T75mTwLwtww0GvSnoyH-VAB8aSDDUKZ8I8.mp4?_nc_cat=1